# Pull requests

When opening a pull request, provide only the pull request title and description.

Do not pre-populate the merge commit message or the extended description. Leave those fields empty so GitHub uses its default.

Do not put the pull request title or description into a merge or squash commit. Do not pass a commit title or commit message when merging.

Still provide a title and description for the pull request itself.

## How to create the PR (required)

Create the PR with the GitHub CLI so **both** title and body are stored on
GitHub. Do **not** rely on the compare-page / “open in GitHub UI” flow that
only carries the title into the browser and leaves the body in chat.

```bash
gh pr create --title "type(scope): imperative description" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary
- ...

## Test plan
- [ ] ...

EOF
)"
```

- Pass the body via a HEREDOC (`<<'EOF'`) so markdown and blank lines survive.
- Prefer `gh pr create` (API create) over `gh pr create --web` or a
  `compare/...` URL unless `gh` cannot authenticate.
- If `gh` returns 403 on create, the token needs `pull_requests: write`; ask
  the user to fix auth rather than pasting a body-only message into chat.
